---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Gruntz handles training data, permissions, subscriptions, and support information for the current mobile app."
  kicker="Privacy Policy"
>
  <p>
    Gruntz is a local-first mobile fitness app focused on tactical-style training missions,
    progress, and subscription-gated premium content. This Privacy Policy describes what data the
    current version of Gruntz may process, how that information is used, and when it may be shared
    with service providers.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    Effective date: {site.updated}. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
  </div>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    Gruntz is local-first. Your progress and settings are stored on the device, and no account is
    required to train. The one exception is progress backup, which you can turn on yourself and is
    described below; when it is off, nothing you log leaves your phone.
  </p>

  <h3>Information stored on the device</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Profile and onboarding selections.</li>
    <li>Program choice, week state, and assessment inputs.</li>
    <li>Mission history, streaks, XP, achievements, and related progress metrics.</li>
    <li>Settings such as notification preferences, reminders, and theme preferences.</li>
    <li>Locally saved subscription state used to reflect entitlement status inside the app.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Permissions and fitness data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Location permission may be requested when you choose to track a run or ruck session.</li>
    <li>
      Motion-related sensors, including pedometer and barometer where available, may be used to
      support workout or run-tracker metrics.
    </li>
    <li>Notification permission may be requested for daily reminders and mission-status alerts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Optional account and progress backup</h3>
  <p>
    Gruntz does not require an account. Training works fully offline and always will. If you
    choose to turn on progress backup from the Profile tab, the following applies:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      We collect your <strong>email address</strong>, and use it only to send you a one-time
      sign-in code and to identify your backup. There is no password, and we do not send
      marketing email.
    </li>
    <li>
      A copy of your <strong>training history and app progress</strong> — logged workouts,
      streaks, achievements, plan state, check-ins and settings — is uploaded so it can be
      restored if you lose, break or replace your phone.
    </li>
    <li>
      Backups are stored with Supabase, our database provider, and protected by row-level
      security so that a backup is readable and writable only by the account that created it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your subscription and entitlement status is <strong>not</strong> included in the backup.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can delete your backup, or delete your entire account, at any time from inside the app
    (Profile → Back up progress). Deleting your account permanently removes your email address
    and your stored backup from our servers. See <a href="#retention">Data Retention</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Purchase and subscription data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Subscription, entitlement, and transaction-related information may be processed through
      RevenueCat and the app-store platform you use.
    </li>
    <li>
      Apple App Store or Google Play may process store account, billing, receipt, and renewal data
      under their own policies.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Deliver the core mission flow, progress system, and training reference content.</li>
    <li>Store and restore your local workout history, streaks, achievements, and preferences.</li>
    <li>Enable run-tracking or motion-driven workout features when you choose to use them.</li>
    <li>Send reminders or mission alerts when notifications are enabled.</li>
    <li>Determine premium access status and restore purchases.</li>
    <li>Send a one-time sign-in code to your email address, if you enable progress backup.</li>
    <li>Store and restore your backed-up training history, if you enable progress backup.</li>
    <li>Respond to support requests you send to us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Sharing and Service Providers</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information from the current Gruntz app, and the current build does
    not include third-party advertising SDKs.
  </p>
  <p>We may rely on the following categories of third parties to operate the app:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>RevenueCat for subscription and entitlement management.</li>
    <li>
      Supabase for optional account sign-in and progress backup storage, and Resend for delivering
      sign-in code emails — both only if you enable progress backup.
    </li>
    <li>Apple App Store or Google Play for payment processing and store-managed subscriptions.</li>
    <li>
      Platform-level services used by the operating system to deliver notifications and fitness
      permissions.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="retention">4. Data Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Local app data remains on your device until you delete it, remove the app, or clear device
    storage. Subscription and purchase records handled by RevenueCat, Apple, or Google may be
    retained according to those providers’ legal and operational requirements.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you enable progress backup, your email address and your most recent backup are retained
    until you delete them. You can delete your backup, or delete your account entirely, from
    Profile → Back up progress inside the app. Deleting your account removes your email address
    and your backup from our servers permanently and cannot be undone; the copy of your training
    on your own phone is left untouched.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use the storage and security features available in the app stack, including local device
    storage and secure storage for sensitive configuration where appropriate. No method of storage
    or transmission is perfectly secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Children’s Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Gruntz is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly design the service for
    child-directed data collection. If you believe a child has provided personal information through
    support or another direct channel, contact us and we will review the request.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your Choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can decline optional permissions such as notifications or location access.</li>
    <li>You can cancel subscriptions through Apple App Store or Google Play account settings.</li>
    <li>You can remove locally stored app data by deleting the app or clearing device data.</li>
    <li>
      You can leave progress backup turned off entirely, or turn it on and later delete your
      backup or your whole account from inside the app.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Future Updates</h2>
  <p>
    If Gruntz adds new integrations, analytics tooling, or health platform sync in a future
    release, this policy may change to reflect those features. The latest version of the policy
    will always be posted on this page with an updated effective date.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy, support, or data handling can be sent to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
